  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A$ be the point $(0,4)$ and $B$ be a moving point on $x$-axis. Let $M$ be the midpoint of $A B$ and let the perpendicular bisector of $A B$ meets the $y$-axis at $R$. The locus of the midpoint $P$ of $M R$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$y+x^{2}=2$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$x^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$(y-2)^{2}-x^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$x^{2}+y^{2}=16$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let B $=(2 \\alpha, 0)$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{M}=(\\alpha, 2)$\r\n$\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{AB}}=\\frac{4}{-2 \\alpha}=-\\frac{2}{\\alpha}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{MR}}=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}, \\therefore \\mathrm{MR} \\quad \\mathrm{y}-2=\\frac{\\alpha}{2}(\\mathrm{x}-\\alpha)$\r\nPut, $\\mathrm{x}=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}=2-\\frac{\\alpha^{2}}{2}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{R} \\equiv\\left(0,2-\\frac{\\alpha^{2}}{2}\\right)$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{P} \\equiv\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}, \\frac{2-\\alpha^{2} / 2+2}{2}\\right) \\equiv \\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}, 2-\\frac{\\alpha^{2}}{4}\\right)$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{y}=2-\\mathrm{x}^{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}+\\mathrm{x}^{2}=2$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0021_3735f74a67c3.png\">"
  }
